  <div class="page-hero">
    <span class="kicker" data-i18n="ts.kicker">Legal</span>
    <h1 data-i18n="ts.title">Terms of Sale</h1>
  </div>
  <div class="section">
    <div class="prose">
      <p class="muted small" data-i18n="ts.updated">Last updated: 7 October 2026.</p>

      <p data-i18n-html="ts.intro"><%- fillVat(pageI18nEn)["ts.intro"] %></p>

      <h2 data-i18n="ts.s1.h">Products</h2>
      <p data-i18n="ts.s1.p"><%- fillVat(pageI18nEn)["ts.s1.p"] %></p>

      <h2 data-i18n="ts.nr.h">Second-hand books: no returns</h2>
      <p data-i18n="ts.nr.p">Used books: no returns or exchanges for a change of mind in the shop. The legal guarantees still apply, and so does the statutory right of withdrawal where the law provides for it. Each book is sold as described: its condition grade is its description, so please read it, and ask us if you have any question. This does not affect your legal rights as a consumer, including the right of withdrawal, where the law provides for it, described below, and the legal guarantees.</p>

